30:Represent the initial schedule as the function plus one kernel record per fusion group. Import the stage 3b plan including its term buffers, aliases and gate. Re-deriving fusion with new passes would duplicate a tested legality analysis. Carry block width policy into the schedule. Singleton schedules start with one thread per element. Stage 2 selects all singleton schedules and omits subsequent optimizations.
120:The first tiled route materialized every member separately. Attention took 0.533 ms and MLP 0.383 ms in single calls. Reusing row placement between the two attention dots and retaining GELU inside the first MLP tile removed three and one launches respectively. At the specified shapes attention executes score, one fused normalization phase, then the value dot. MLP executes hidden projection plus GELU, then the output projection. The original one-block-per-row route and its original per-statement fallback remain executable. For these row groups, the existing gates field reports whether the original fused-row route ran. On the tiled route it reports unfused even where individual phases fuse several statements. For scheduled singletons it distinguishes the optimized and original element routes. [Initial check](../scripts/02-check.jsonl) · [First fused phases](../scripts/02-phases.jsonl)
128:## Exact check and cost
130:The final checker compares output shape and every f32 word against the current revision, with NaNs compared as a class. It forces the original fused and unfused sides, the tiled phase route for row groups, and the wide specialization where present. The baseline key includes the Tix revision, function name and mode inventory used by the recipe. The base's signed, positive, half-ULP, signed-zero, mixed-shape and empty cases remain. For recognized dots it also requests one signed full 64×64×32 panel case where the shape bindings and the existing sampling budget permit. Dedicated GPU tests cover a complete 128-square wide tile, both transposed operands, ragged panels, K=1, K=0, and register epilogues. Changing one lane of a packed load in the aligned branch produced a numerical counterexample.
134:All six cold checks accepted under the exact relation. These are wall times for one cold check and its immediate replay per program. Pipeline time measures a separate host compilation into a CUDA-source artifact. The last column sums CUDA events across all cases of the cold check. Replays recompute the recipe and f32 references and submitted zero GPU batches. [Cost measurement](../scripts/14-contract-cost.jsonl)
147:- Performance is measured at the listed shapes and selected boundary cases. Those observations and fallback identity support the no-regression result on the measured set. They do not prove a latency bound over all possible shapes, contention or driver versions.

